# Request collection for the service, in the plain-text .http format that
# editors such as VS Code (REST Client) and JetBrains IDEs run.
# Start the service first (make start), then send a request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Liveness probe: 200 with the body "pong"
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### Health check: 204 without a body, or a 500 problem document that lists the failing dependencies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### List the resources, newest first; page starts at 1, itemsPerPage is 1 to 100 (a bare JSON array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources?page=1&itemsPerPage=30

### Create a resource: 201 with the resource and a location header; 422 when validation fails
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example name",
  "description": "Example description"
}

### Retrieve one resource by identifier: 200, 400 for an invalid identifier, 404 when it does not exist
# Replace the identifier with the id returned by the create request.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/example_api_resources/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe

### GraphQL query: one page of resources (page and itemsPerPage have defaults)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($page: Int!, $itemsPerPage: Int!) { exampleApiResources(page: $page, itemsPerPage: $itemsPerPage) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "page": 1, "itemsPerPage": 30 }
}

### GraphQL query: one resource by id (null when it does not exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { exampleApiResource(id: $id) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe" }
}

### GraphQL mutation: create a resource
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateExampleApiResourceInput!) { createExampleApiResource(input: $input) { id name description } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "name": "Example name", "description": "Example description" } }
}

### IAM (authorization/iam): the health check shows that the service runs with the IAM context wired: 204, or a 500 problem document that lists the failing dependencies.
# Every IAM operation requires a bearer token; each one adds its requests to this section.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Resolve a User service token over REST: 200 with the subject, or resolved = false with the token reason code; 401 without a valid bearer token
# Replace both tokens: the bearer token of the caller (a user token, or a service token that names the IAM caller audience) and the credential to resolve.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/token-resolutions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "<token to resolve>"
}

### Resolve a User service token over GraphQL: the same answer as the REST operation; the error code UNAUTHENTICATED without a valid bearer token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($credential: String!) { resolveToken(input: { credential: $credential }) { resolved reason subjectId subjectKind sessionId roles expiresAt } }",
  "variables": { "credential": "<token to resolve>" }
}

### Validate access over REST: 200 with a decision body (allow, or deny with the reason and the denied keys), whatever the subject's rights; 422 for no target form, two target forms, more than 100 keys or a minPolicyVersion above the current policy version; 401 without a valid bearer token
# Replace both tokens: the bearer token of the caller and the credential of the subject. Send exactly one of "rest", "graphql" and "permissions".
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/access-validations
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "<subject token>",
  "service": "billing",
  "rest": {
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/api/invoices/42"
  },
  "requestId": "req-0001"
}

### Validate permission keys over REST: the same decision body; "scopes" is "all" or the project ids that hold every key
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/access-validations
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "<subject token>",
  "service": "billing",
  "permissions": ["rest:billing:GET /api/invoices"],
  "projectId": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890cd",
  "requestId": "req-0002"
}

### Validate a GraphQL document over REST: allowed only when the subject holds every coordinate it selects; "denied" lists every coordinate it does not hold; a document over a limit (64 KiB, depth 15, 500 coordinates, 50 aliases, 100 fragments) is a deny with the reason limits_exceeded
# "operationName" is optional when the document holds exactly one operation.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/access-validations
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "<subject token>",
  "service": "billing",
  "graphql": {
    "document": "query GetInvoice { invoice { id total } }",
    "operationName": "GetInvoice"
  },
  "requestId": "req-0004"
}

### Validate a GraphQL document over GraphQL: the same decision as the REST operation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($input: ValidateAccessInput!) { validateAccess(input: $input) { decision reason denied scopes { all projects } subject { id kind } decisionId policyVersion requestId } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "credential": "<subject token>",
      "service": "billing",
      "graphql": { "document": "query GetInvoice { invoice { id total } }", "operationName": "GetInvoice" },
      "requestId": "req-0005"
    }
  }
}

### Validate access over GraphQL: the same decision as the REST operation; the error code VALIDATION_FAILED for an invalid request, UNAUTHENTICATED without a valid bearer token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($input: ValidateAccessInput!) { validateAccess(input: $input) { decision reason denied scopes { all projects } subject { id kind } decisionId policyVersion requestId } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "credential": "<subject token>",
      "service": "billing",
      "rest": { "method": "GET", "path": "/api/invoices/42" },
      "requestId": "req-0003"
    }
  }
}

### Validate a batch of checks over REST: 200 with one result per check in request order, each with its own decisionId; a check that cannot be read is a deny with the reason malformed_operation and does not fail the others; each distinct credential is resolved once per batch; 422 for no check or more than 100; 401 without a valid bearer token
# Replace both tokens: the bearer token of the caller and the credential of each check. Each check has the shape of the single check.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/access-validations/batch
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "checks": [
    {
      "credential": "<subject token>",
      "service": "billing",
      "rest": { "method": "GET", "path": "/api/invoices/42" },
      "requestId": "req-0101"
    },
    {
      "credential": "<subject token>",
      "service": "billing",
      "permissions": ["rest:billing:GET /api/invoices"],
      "requestId": "req-0102"
    }
  ]
}

### Validate a batch of checks over GraphQL: the same results as the REST operation; the error code VALIDATION_FAILED for no input or more than 100, UNAUTHENTICATED without a valid bearer token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($inputs: [ValidateAccessInput!]!) { validateAccessBatch(inputs: $inputs) { decision reason denied scopes { all projects } subject { id kind } decisionId policyVersion requestId } }",
  "variables": {
    "inputs": [
      {
        "credential": "<subject token>",
        "service": "billing",
        "rest": { "method": "GET", "path": "/api/invoices/42" },
        "requestId": "req-0103"
      },
      {
        "credential": "<subject token>",
        "service": "billing",
        "permissions": ["rest:billing:GET /api/invoices"],
        "requestId": "req-0104"
      }
    ]
  }
}

### Create a role over REST: 201 with Location, ETag, the id and version 1; 409 for a duplicate name; 422 for an invalid name or a reused Idempotency-Key; 401 without a valid bearer token
# A repeated Idempotency-Key with the same body within 24 hours returns the original result and creates nothing again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: create-billing-administrator
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Billing administrator",
  "description": "Manages invoices and refunds."
}

### Create a role over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes CONFLICT, VALIDATION_FAILED and UNAUTHENTICATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateRoleInput!) { createRole(input: $input) { id name description kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "name": "Billing administrator", "description": "Manages invoices and refunds.", "idempotencyKey": "create-billing-administrator" } }
}

### Wait for the Kafka acknowledgement of a write: 200, 201 or 204 with Iam-Policy-Version and Iam-Policy-Offset once the version is published, or 202 with Iam-Propagation-Status committed_pending_propagation when PUBLISH_WAIT_TIMEOUT passes first; wait=propagated is refused with 422 until Story 13.4
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe/permissions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
If-Match: "1"
Prefer: wait=published
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "keys": []
}

### The same wait over GraphQL: the consistency input (PUBLISHED, the default, or PROPAGATED) and the propagation field of the payload; the status is PUBLISHED or COMMITTED_PENDING
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: SetRolePermissionsInput!) { setRolePermissions(input: $input) { id version propagation { status policyVersion podsAcknowledged podsTimedOut } } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "expectedVersion": 1, "keys": [], "consistency": "PUBLISHED" } }
}

### Get a role over REST: 200 with its ETag, 404 for an unknown id, 422 for an id that is not a UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Get a role over GraphQL: null for an unknown id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { role(id: $id) { id name description kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe" }
}

### Update a role over REST: 200 with the new ETag; 428 without If-Match; 412 for a stale If-Match; 403 for a system role; 404 for an unknown id; 409 for a duplicate name; 422 for invalid fields
# The If-Match header carries the ETag of the version read. A null description removes it and an absent member keeps it.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
If-Match: "1"
Idempotency-Key: rename-billing-administrator
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Accounting administrator",
  "description": null
}

### Update a role over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes PRECONDITION_REQUIRED, PRECONDITION_FAILED, FORBIDDEN, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: UpdateRoleInput!) { updateRole(input: $input) { id name description kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "expectedVersion": 1, "name": "Accounting administrator" } }
}

### Delete a role over REST: 200 with the final ETag, the Iam-Policy-Version and the number of assignments it revoked; 428 without If-Match; 412 for a stale If-Match; 403 for a system role; 404 for an unknown or deleted role; 202 with the Location of a bulk operation for a role with more assignments than BULK_CHUNK_ENTITIES
# Every assignment of the role is revoked in the same transaction. A replay with the same Idempotency-Key returns the original count. A role with more assignments than BULK_CHUNK_ENTITIES is deleted by a bulk operation instead: the 202 response carries its Location, revokedAssignments is the number it will revoke, and the runner commits the revocations in versions of at most BULK_CHUNK_ENTITIES entities before it deletes the role.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
If-Match: "1"
Idempotency-Key: delete-billing-administrator

### Delete a role over GraphQL: the id, the final version, the policy version and revokedAssignments, and bulkOperationId (null unless the role has more assignments than BULK_CHUNK_ENTITIES); the error codes PRECONDITION_REQUIRED, PRECONDITION_FAILED, FORBIDDEN and NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: DeleteRoleInput!) { deleteRole(input: $input) { id version policyVersion revokedAssignments bulkOperationId } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "expectedVersion": 1 } }
}

### Read a bulk operation over REST: its kind, status, applied and total records, the policy versions of its first and last chunk, its requester and propagation (null until the chunks of a revocation-class operation are fenced); 404 for an unknown id, 422 for an id that is not a UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bulk-operations/0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890af
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### List the bulk operations over REST: oldest first with a cursor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bulk-operations?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read and list bulk operations over GraphQL: bulkOperation(id) is null for an unknown id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { bulkOperation(id: $id) { id kind status totalRecords appliedRecords firstVersion lastVersion requester error propagation { status policyVersion podsAcknowledged podsTimedOut } } bulkOperations(first: 20) { items { id status } nextCursor } }",
  "variables": { "id": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890af" }
}

### Resync the policy state over REST: republishes the complete current policy as a new log epoch, with versions above the highest version of the state topic, as a bulk operation of kind resync; needs iam:policy:resync, 202 with the Location of the bulk operation, 422 without a reason or for a reused Idempotency-Key, 403 without the key, 409 for a policy without entities
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/policy-resyncs
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: resync-2027-01-15

{
  "reason": "The state topic lost records after a broker failure."
}

### Resync the policy state over GraphQL: the mutation returns the bulk operation; a repeated idempotencyKey with the same input returns the original operation and starts no second resync
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: ResyncPolicyInput!) { resyncPolicy(input: $input) { id kind status totalRecords appliedRecords firstVersion lastVersion } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "reason": "The state topic lost records after a broker failure.", "idempotencyKey": "resync-2027-01-15" } }
}

### Read the permissions of a role over REST: every grant in key order with its key, kind (rest, gql or reserved), service, active flag and wildcard flag, and the ETag of the role; 404 for an unknown role, 422 for an id that is not a UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe/permissions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Replace the permissions of a role over REST: keys of an active catalogue and the four wildcard forms of a service that has a catalogue, at most 5000; If-Match is required (428 without it, 412 when stale); unknown keys are 422 with one violation per key; the change takes the next policy version and records iam.role_permissions.changed; an added wildcard is audited with coversFutureElements=true
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe/permissions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
If-Match: "1"
Idempotency-Key: set-billing-permissions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "keys": ["rest:billing:GET /invoices", "gql:billing:Query.invoices", "gql:billing:*"]
}

### Read and replace the permissions of a role over GraphQL: Role.permissions lists the grants and setRolePermissions returns the changed role; the error codes PRECONDITION_REQUIRED, PRECONDITION_FAILED, NOT_FOUND and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: SetRolePermissionsInput!) { setRolePermissions(input: $input) { id version grantCount permissions { key kind service active wildcard } } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "expectedVersion": 1, "keys": ["rest:billing:GET /invoices", "gql:billing:*"], "idempotencyKey": "set-billing-permissions-gql" } }
}

### List roles over REST: a page of 1 to 100 roles with the nextCursor of the next page, filtered by namePrefix (without regard to case) and kind (system or custom)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles?limit=30&namePrefix=bill&kind=custom
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### List roles over GraphQL: the same page; pass the nextCursor as after for the next page
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($first: Int, $after: String, $filter: RoleFilter) { roles(first: $first, after: $after, filter: $filter) { items { id name kind grantCount version createdAt updatedAt } nextCursor } }",
  "variables": { "first": 30, "filter": { "namePrefix": "bill", "kind": "custom" } }
}

### Load a GraphQL specification over REST: a draft version with its hash, coordinate count and the diff against the active versions (201); the same SDL again returns that version (200). The service iam is reserved (403); a body is limited to 6 MiB (413)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service": "billing",
  "sdl": "type Query {\n  invoices: [Invoice!]!\n}\n\ntype Mutation {\n  pay(id: ID!): Invoice! @iamSensitive\n}\n\ntype Invoice {\n  id: ID!\n}\n"
}

### Load a GraphQL specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes FORBIDDEN and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: LoadGraphqlSpecInput!) { loadGraphqlSpec(input: $input) { id service contentHash status uploadedBy createdAt coordinateCount diff { added removed removedGrants { coordinate roles } wildcardGains { role pattern coordinates } flagDowngrades { coordinate before { sensitive auditAlways } after { sensitive auditAlways } } } } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "service": "billing", "sdl": "type Query { invoices: [String!]! }" } }
}

### Load an OpenAPI specification over REST: a draft version with its hash, operation count and the diff against the active versions (201); the same document again returns that version (200). The document is JSON text of at most 5 MiB with internal references only; a violation carries the JSON pointer of the fault (422). The service iam is reserved (403); a body is limited to 6 MiB (413)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi-specs
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service": "billing",
  "document": "{\"openapi\":\"3.1.0\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Billing\",\"version\":\"1\"},\"paths\":{\"/invoices\":{\"get\":{\"operationId\":\"listInvoices\"}},\"/invoices/{invoiceId}\":{\"post\":{\"operationId\":\"payInvoice\",\"x-iam-sensitive\":true}}}}"
}

### Load an OpenAPI specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes FORBIDDEN and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: LoadOpenapiSpecInput!) { loadOpenapiSpec(input: $input) { id service contentHash status uploadedBy createdAt operationCount diff { added removed removedGrants { operation roles } wildcardGains { role pattern operations } flagDowngrades { operation before { sensitive auditAlways } after { sensitive auditAlways } } } } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "service": "billing", "document": "{\"openapi\":\"3.1.0\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Billing\",\"version\":\"1\"},\"paths\":{\"/invoices\":{\"get\":{}}}}" } }
}

### List GraphQL specifications over REST: one page in a stable order with nextCursor; filters service and status; the SDL only with includeSdl=true; 422 for an invalid parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs?service=billing&status=draft&limit=10&includeSdl=false
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read a GraphQL specification over REST: service, hash, status, uploader, timestamps and coordinate count; the SDL only with includeSdl=true; 404 for an unknown version
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd?includeSdl=true
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read the diff of a GraphQL specification over REST: the added and removed coordinates, the removed coordinates that roles grant, the wildcard grants that gain coordinates and the flag downgrades such as a dropped @iamSensitive; 404 for an unknown version
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd/diff
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Activate a GraphQL specification over REST: the draft becomes active and its fields grantable permissions (201 with the created keys and the policy version); an active version returns 200 and changes nothing. 409 lists the keys that would lose a flag until confirmFlagDowngrade is true and the grants that would be orphaned until confirmOrphans is true; renames move the grants of an old key to its new key; a repeated Idempotency-Key with the same body returns the original result
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd/permissions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: activate-billing-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confirmOrphans": false,
  "confirmFlagDowngrade": false,
  "renames": [{ "from": "gql:billing:Query.bills", "to": "gql:billing:Query.invoices" }]
}

### Activate a GraphQL specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes FLAG_DOWNGRADE_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, ORPHAN_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, CONFLICT, NOT_FOUND and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateGraphqlPermissionsInput!) { createGraphqlPermissions(input: $input) { id service status createdKeys policyVersion } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd", "confirmOrphans": false, "confirmFlagDowngrade": false, "renames": [], "idempotencyKey": "activate-billing-1" } }
}

### Retire a GraphQL specification over REST: the active version leaves the catalogue of its service unless another active version holds its fields (200 with the policy version and iam.graphql_spec.retired). 409 lists the grants that would be orphaned until confirmOrphans is true; with it the grants become inactive and iam.permissions.orphaned is recorded, and a grant stays inactive when its key returns with a later version until an administrator grants it again; 409 for a version that is not active; a repeated Idempotency-Key with the same body returns the original result
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd/retirement
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: retire-billing-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confirmOrphans": false
}

### Retire a GraphQL specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes ORPHAN_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, CONFLICT, NOT_FOUND and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: RetireGraphqlSpecInput!) { retireGraphqlSpec(input: $input) { id service status policyVersion } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd", "confirmOrphans": false, "idempotencyKey": "retire-billing-1" } }
}

### Read GraphQL specifications over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operations; graphqlSpec is null for an unknown version, and sdl and diff are read only when they are selected
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($filter: GraphqlSpecFilter) { graphqlSpecs(first: 10, filter: $filter) { items { id service contentHash status uploadedBy createdAt activatedAt retiredAt coordinateCount diff { added removed removedGrants { coordinate roles } wildcardGains { role pattern coordinates } flagDowngrades { coordinate before { sensitive auditAlways } after { sensitive auditAlways } } } } nextCursor } }",
  "variables": { "filter": { "service": "billing", "status": "draft" } }
}

### Read one GraphQL specification over GraphQL, with its SDL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { graphqlSpec(id: $id) { id service status coordinateCount sdl diff { removed removedGrants { coordinate roles } } } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd" }
}

### List GraphQL permissions over REST: one page of the catalogue in a stable order with nextCursor; filters service, type, active, sensitive and keyPrefix; each entry shows its key, service, type, field, flags, active state, the active versions that contain it and the roles that grant it by its exact key; 422 for an invalid parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-permissions?service=billing&type=Mutation&active=true&sensitive=true&keyPrefix=gql:billing:Mutation.&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read a GraphQL permission over REST: the same entry as a list item; 404 for an unknown permission, 422 for an identifier that is not a UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql-permissions/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### List GraphQL permissions over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; pass the nextCursor as after for the next page
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($first: Int, $after: String, $filter: GraphqlPermissionFilter) { graphqlPermissions(first: $first, after: $after, filter: $filter) { items { id key service type field flags { sensitive auditAlways } active versions roles } nextCursor } }",
  "variables": { "first": 10, "filter": { "service": "billing", "type": "Mutation", "active": true, "sensitive": true, "keyPrefix": "gql:billing:Mutation." } }
}

### Read one GraphQL permission over GraphQL: graphqlPermission is null for an unknown permission
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($id: ID!) { graphqlPermission(id: $id) { id key service type field flags { sensitive auditAlways } active versions roles } }",
  "variables": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe" }
}

### List OpenAPI specifications over REST: one page in a stable order with nextCursor; filters service and status; the document only with includeDocument=true; 422 for an invalid parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi-specs?service=billing&status=draft&limit=10&includeDocument=false
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read an OpenAPI specification over REST: service, hash, status, uploader, timestamps and operation count; the document only with includeDocument=true; 404 for an unknown version
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd?includeDocument=true
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read the diff of an OpenAPI specification over REST: the added and removed operations, the removed operations that roles grant, the wildcard grants that gain operations and the flag downgrades such as a dropped x-iam-sensitive; 404 for an unknown version
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd/diff
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Activate an OpenAPI specification over REST: the draft becomes active and its operations grantable permissions with keys such as rest:billing:GET /invoices (201 with the created keys and the policy version); an active version returns 200 and changes nothing. 409 lists the keys that would lose a flag until confirmFlagDowngrade is true and the grants that would be orphaned until confirmOrphans is true; renames move the grants of an old key to its new key; a repeated Idempotency-Key with the same body returns the original result
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd/permissions
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: activate-billing-operations-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confirmOrphans": false,
  "confirmFlagDowngrade": false,
  "renames": [{ "from": "rest:billing:GET /bills", "to": "rest:billing:GET /invoices" }]
}

### Activate an OpenAPI specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes FLAG_DOWNGRADE_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, ORPHAN_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, CONFLICT, NOT_FOUND and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: CreateRestPermissionsInput!) { createRestPermissions(input: $input) { id service status createdKeys policyVersion } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd", "confirmOrphans": false, "confirmFlagDowngrade": false, "renames": [], "idempotencyKey": "activate-billing-operations-1" } }
}

### Retire an OpenAPI specification over REST: the active version leaves the catalogue of its service unless another active version holds its operations (200 with the policy version and iam.openapi_spec.retired). 409 lists the grants that would be orphaned until confirmOrphans is true; with it the grants become inactive and iam.permissions.orphaned is recorded, and a grant stays inactive when its key returns with a later version until an administrator grants it again; 409 for a version that is not active; a repeated Idempotency-Key with the same body returns the original result
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi-specs/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd/retirement
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: retire-billing-operations-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confirmOrphans": false
}

### Retire an OpenAPI specification over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes ORPHAN_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, CONFLICT, NOT_FOUND and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: RetireOpenapiSpecInput!) { retireOpenapiSpec(input: $input) { id service status policyVersion } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "id": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfd", "confirmOrphans": false, "idempotencyKey": "retire-billing-operations-1" } }
}

