### Assign a role over REST: 201 with Location, ETag and Iam-Policy-Version; 409 for a duplicate assignment; 422 for an invalid value, an unknown role (roleId) or a past expiry (expiresAt)
# The subject is a user (a UUID) or a service (a service name such as billing-worker); the scope is global or a project (with projectId). A role that grants a wildcard or an iam: key also records iam.privileged_role.assigned.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user-roles
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: assign-billing-administrator
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": { "kind": "user", "id": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890ab" },
  "roleId": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe",
  "scope": { "kind": "project", "projectId": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890cd" },
  "expiresAt": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### Assign a role over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes CONFLICT and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation ($input: AssignUserRoleInput!) { assignUserRole(input: $input) { id subject { kind id } roleId roleName scope { kind projectId } expiresAt version createdAt updatedAt } }",
  "variables": { "input": { "subject": { "kind": "service", "id": "billing-worker" }, "roleId": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe", "scope": { "kind": "global" } } }
}

### Read the effective permissions of a user over REST: 200 with every held key and wildcard, its granting roles, scopes (all or project ids), shortest expiry and the policyVersion; 403 without the key of the operation; 422 for an invalid userId, projectId or service
# projectId keeps the global assignments and those of the project; service keeps the keys and wildcards of the service. Expired assignments grant nothing and a reserved iam: key counts only through a global assignment, as in a decision.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890ab/role-permissions?projectId=0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890cd&service=billing
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read the effective permissions of a user over GraphQL: the same data as the REST operation; the error codes FORBIDDEN and VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/graphql
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($userId: ID!, $projectId: String, $service: String) { userRolePermissions(userId: $userId, projectId: $projectId, service: $service) { userId policyVersion permissions { key kind service wildcard scopes expiresAt roles { id name } } } }",
  "variables": { "userId": "0190f2a8-7b3c-7d4e-8f10-1234567890ab", "service": "billing" }
}

### Read an assignment over REST: 200 with the ETag and the role name; 404 for an unknown or revoked assignment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-roles/01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facff
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>

### Read an assignment over GraphQL: null for an unknown or revoked assignment
