### Create a route over REST: 201 with Location, ETag and Iam-Policy-Version; the caller needs iam:route:{service} or iam:route:* (403 otherwise) and iam:route:anonymous for an anonymous or audit-only route (403 otherwise, audited); the service must equal the catalogService of the upstream (422); 409 for a route that overlaps another route of its host, for a candidate route table that the gateway could not build (route-table-conflict) and for a route of the service iam (system-entry, audited); 422 for an unknown upstream or rate policy, an invalid pattern or an origin that is not exact; the flags default to false, enforcement to enforce, bodyLimitBytes to 1048576, requestTimeoutMs to 30000, idleTimeoutMs to 60000 and retryPolicy to none
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer <caller token>
Idempotency-Key: create-orders-route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "host": "app.example.test",
  "methods": ["GET", "PATCH"],
  "pathPattern": "/api/orders/{id}",
  "service": "core",
  "upstreamId": "01a1c6b5-cb86-7134-868a-7608036facfe",
  "cors": {
    "origins": ["https://app.example.test"],
    "methods": ["GET"],
    "headers": ["content-type"],
    "allowCredentials": true,
    "maxAgeSeconds": 600
  }
}

